=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# firewall refusals --------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Mock: The refusals before asking, each the control's: Install$
# finding no package or changing others, no ss, ss failing,$
# sshd's configuration not in effect, ufw's state not read,$
# ENABLED and the chains disagreeing, a saved blocklist, a saved$
# deny, IPv6 off in ufw, a one-family allowlist, an active deny,$
# Proxmox VE not established; then Apply on an inactive ufw.$
$
# item 1, apt finds no ufw -------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# hardn can't find ufw in apt's package lists. Run apt-get$
# update, then try again.$
$
# item 1, apk finds no ufw -------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# hardn can't find ufw in apk's package lists. Check the network$
# and the community repository, run apk update, then try again.$
$
# item 1, other packages change --------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# Installing ufw would also change other packages: nftables.$
# Install it by hand, then try again.$
$
# item 1, no ss ------------------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# hardn can't tell which ports SSH uses: ss isn't installed.$
# Install iproute2, then try again.$
$
# item 1, ss failing -------------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# hardn can't tell which ports SSH uses: ss failed. Check that$
# it runs, then try again.$
$
# item 1, sshd's configuration not in effect -------------------$
$
# Warning$
# sshd isn't listening where its config says, so hardn can't$
# tell which ports SSH uses. Reload sshd or restart ssh.socket,$
# then try again.$
$
# item 1, bound elsewhere, inactive ----------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# sshd isn't listening where its config says, so hardn can't$
# tell which ports SSH uses. Reload sshd or restart ssh.socket,$
# then try again.$
$
# item 1, ufw's state not read ---------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# hardn can't read ufw's state. Check ufw status verbose, then$
# try again.$
$
# item 1, lockout-at-start -------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# ufw is set to start at boot but isn't running. Check that its$
# rules let SSH through, then run ufw enable.$
$
# item 1, blocklist --------------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# A saved ufw rule would block SSH on port 22, for some$
# addresses or all. Remove it with ufw delete, then try again.$
$
# item 1, a saved deny -----------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# A saved ufw rule would block SSH on port 22, for some$
# addresses or all. Remove it with ufw delete, then try again.$
$
# item 1, IPv6 off in ufw --------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# ufw's IPv6 is off in /etc/default/ufw, so it would refuse SSH$
# on port 22. Set IPV6=yes, then try again.$
$
# item 1, IPv6 off in ufw, active ------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# ufw's IPv6 is off in /etc/default/ufw, so it would refuse SSH$
# on port 22. Set IPV6=yes, then try again.$
$
# item 1, an allowlist of one family ---------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# ufw refuses SSH on [::]:22, and hardn doesn't change a rule it$
# finds. Fix it with ufw allow or ufw delete, then try again.$
$
# item 1, an active deny ---------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# ufw refuses SSH on [::]:22, and hardn doesn't change a rule it$
# finds. Fix it with ufw allow or ufw delete, then try again.$
$
# item 1, Proxmox VE not established ---------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# hardn can't tell if this host runs Proxmox VE, where it leaves$
# the firewall alone.$
$
# Apply, ufw inactive ------------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# ufw isn't running, so hardn saves no rule for it. Enable the$
# firewall, then apply.$
$
$

